From: xinyang <xinyang@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] camera: keep still capture on top of the upstream tree

The upstream camera only records frames under an FRAME_SYNC strobe
window. Without a subscription the strobe path cannot time a pulse, so a
still is taken from a settled preview stream instead: run the largest
native mode, let auto exposure adapt, copy one packed NV12 frame, and
restore the preview. The record carries its own flag and omits the
exposure and line-time fields that only a strobe frame has.

The lens is resolved through the sensor's ancillary link rather than by
driver name, so an actuator change does not break focus.

---
